      // row. Fix = a real per-face bounce (flip vy on a top/bottom hit, vx on a
      // side hit) plus pushing the ball back out of the brick.
    }
```

To fix this, I need to determine which side of the brick the ball hit and flip the corresponding velocity component. I also need to "push" the ball out of the brick to prevent it from getting stuck inside or triggering multiple collisions in subsequent frames if it's moving slowly.

The `collides` function is a simple AABB test:

```javascript
export function collides(ball, brick) {
  return (
    ball.x + ball.r > brick.x &&
    ball.x - ball.r < brick.x + brick.w &&
    ball.y + ball.r > brick.y &&
    ball.y - ball.r < brick.y + brick.h
  );
}
```

To implement a per-face bounce, I can check the overlap on each side. A common way to do this for AABB-Circle (or in this case, Circle approximated by AABB) collision is to find the distance between the center of the ball and the center of the brick, and then compare the overlap on the X and Y axes.

Let's refine the collision logic.

Ball center: `(ball.x, ball.y)`
Ball bounds: `[ball.x - ball.r, ball.x + ball.r]` x `[ball.y - ball.r, ball.y + ball.r]`
Brick bounds: `[brick.x, brick.x + brick.w]` x `[brick.y, brick.y + brick.h]`

Overlap on X:
`overlapX = min(ball.x + ball.r, brick.x + brick.w) - max(ball.x - ball.r, brick.x)`
Overlap on Y:
`overlapY = min(ball.y + ball.r, brick.y + brick.h) - max(ball.y - ball.r, brick.y)`

The side hit is the one with the smaller overlap.

If `overlapX < overlapY`:
  If `ball.x < brick.x + brick.w / 2`, it hit the left side.
  If `ball.x > brick.x + brick.w / 2`, it hit the right side.
  Flip `ball.vx`.

If `overlapY < overlapX`:
  If `ball.y < brick.y + brick.h / 2`, it hit the top side.
  If `ball.y > brick.y + brick.h / 2`, it hit the bottom side.
  Flip `ball.vy`.

Wait, the current `collides` function is used inside `frame` which is called every frame.

Actually, a simpler way to implement the bounce and push-out:

```javascript
    if (collides(state.ball, brick)) {
      brick.alive = false;
      state.combo += 1;
      state.score += scoreForBrick(brick, state.combo);

      // Bounce logic
      const ballLeft = state.ball.x - state.ball.r;
      const ballRight = state.ball.x + state.ball.r;
      const ballTop = state.ball.y - state.ball.r;
      const ballBottom = state.ball.y + state.ball.r;

      const brickLeft = brick.x;
      const brickRight = brick.x + brick.w;
      const brickTop = brick.y;
      const brickBottom = brick.y + brick.h;

      const overlapX = Math.min(ballRight, brickRight) - Math.max(ballLeft, brickLeft);
      const overlapY = Math.min(ballBottom, brickBottom) - Math.max(ballTop, brickTop);

      if (overlapX < overlapY) {
        state.ball.vx = -state.ball.vx;
        // Push out
        if (state.ball.x < brick.x + brick.w / 2) {
          state.ball.x = brickLeft - state.ball.r;
        } else {
          state.ball.x = brickRight + state.ball.r;
        }
      } else {
        state.ball.vy = -state.ball.vy;
        // Push out
        if (state.ball.y < brick.y + brick.h / 2) {
          state.ball.y = brickTop - state.ball.r;
        } else {
          state.ball.y = brickBottom + state.ball.r;
        }
      }
    }
```

